# A guarded table's row policy is asked on every path that reaches the table,
# as the caller the task acts for, so no path has more rights than its
# caller's. The fixture's notes are each their owner's alone. eve, who owns
# none, reads and writes the table directly, binds a live query, spawns a
# task as a job's worker is spawned, calls a public and a signed-in endpoint,
# and sends a webhook delivery under a guessed key. A task that acts for no
# one, the program's own included, does the same. A live binding runs as the
# caller that bound it even when another caller reads it; a spawned task and
# a request act for no one, whoever spawned or served them; a signed-in
# endpoint answers 401 while no request has a signed-in caller. Every one of
# those attempts is refused or finds nothing. Only a run that asks for the
# system reads every note.
fixture: RowPolicyNoBypass.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = row_policy_no_bypass.stdout.expected
